# LINE ENDINGS, SO THAT A MEASUREMENT MEANS SOMETHING.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the machine this was written on and there was no
# .gitattributes, so every checkout — including the ones git does internally for
# `stash push` and `stash pop` — rewrote the working copy of any file it touched
# to CRLF. Committed content was never affected (git normalises on the way in)
# and `git diff` stayed honest, but `build.mjs` reads the WORKING TREE, so the
# size it prints moved with whichever files git had last handled.
#
# Measured 31 Aug 2026: the same source built to 8980.4 KB twice, and then to
# 9018.0 KB after a single stash round-trip — 44,236 lines gaining one byte
# each. Any statement about how big this game is needs this file to be true.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...and the things that are not text, so nothing tries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
